WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.659 --> 00:00:04.700
Marvel Studios has shrouded its plans for
the Disney+ streaming service in its usual

00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:08.360
veil of secrecy, but we've already gotten
a pretty good peek at some of the shows in

00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:09.060
development.

00:00:09.140 --> 00:00:11.740
Here's everything we know about their plans
so far.

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:17.520
In November 2018, Disney confirmed a number
of the original series in development including

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:19.720
a Loki series starring Tom Hiddleston.

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:23.390
There were still no details about when the
series would be set, or how it was possible

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:26.010
considering Loki's death in Avengers: Infinity
War.

00:00:26.010 --> 00:00:29.619
We had so many questions, and then came Avengers:
Endgame with an answer.

00:00:29.619 --> 00:00:33.710
When the Avengers go back in time to the events
of 2012's Avengers, they inadvertently give

00:00:33.710 --> 00:00:37.720
Loki the opportunity to steal back the Tesseract
and escape from their custody.

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:42.020
Directors Joe and Anthony Russo confirmed
a few weeks after Endgame's release that the

00:00:42.020 --> 00:00:44.610
Loki of the past created an alternate timeline
when he escaped.

00:00:44.610 --> 00:00:48.170
It hasn't been confirmed that this will be
the version of Loki viewers follow in his

00:00:48.170 --> 00:00:52.220
upcoming limited series, but it certainly
seems like the most likely possibility.

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:57.460
While rumors floated around for a while, it
took until April 2019 for the Scarlet Witch

00:00:57.461 --> 00:01:01.550
series to be confirmed, and once it was, we
learned it wouldn't be just Scarlet Witch.

00:01:01.550 --> 00:01:06.020
During a Disney investors meeting, Kevin Feige
revealed the show would be called WandaVision,

00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:10.330
and would feature the return of not only Elizabeth
Olsen as Scarlet Witch, but Paul Bettany as

00:01:10.330 --> 00:01:11.460
the android Vision as well.

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:14.860
What we know about WandaVision is both intriguing
and a little confusing.

00:01:15.020 --> 00:01:19.700
Vision died in Avengers: Infinity War and,
unlike Scarlet Witch, wasn't revived in Endgame.

00:01:19.760 --> 00:01:25.220
Olsen's talk with Variety later in April revealed
more puzzling details about the show: specifically

00:01:25.220 --> 00:01:28.000
that at least part of it will apparently have
a retro aesthetic.

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:31.540
She dished that the show's story would be
pulled from, quote, "quite a few other comic

00:01:31.540 --> 00:01:35.940
books" and pointed out that, quote, "at the
Disney+ launch chat, they showed a photo of

00:01:35.940 --> 00:01:37.520
[Scarlet Witch and Vision] in the '50s."

00:01:37.640 --> 00:01:43.200
In May 2019, a rumor circulated suggesting
Scarlet Witch's powers will become more comic-book-accurate

00:01:43.210 --> 00:01:46.600
in WandaVision, meaning she'll gain access
to reality-altering abilities.

00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:50.830
While there's been no confirmation, this would
go a long way to explain how Vision is apparently

00:01:50.830 --> 00:01:51.820
coming back to life.

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:53.680
"I'm really sorry.

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:54.180
What?!"

00:01:57.280 --> 00:01:58.880
"You couldn't have done that earlier?"

00:02:00.140 --> 00:02:00.960
"I hate you."

00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:06.520
In October 2018, Variety reported Anthony
Mackie's Falcon and Sebastian Stan's Bucky,

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:10.970
a.k.a. the Winter Soldier, would be partnering
up for their own limited series on Disney+.

00:02:10.970 --> 00:02:15.360
The story claimed it would be the first of
the Disney+ MCU original series to find a

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:18.260
writer, naming Empire producer and writer
Martin Spellman.

00:02:18.420 --> 00:02:23.700
The series, titled Falcon and Winter Soldier,
was confirmed in April 2019, along with WandaVision,

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:25.800
when Kevin Feige addressed Disney investors.

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:29.760
Since then we've learned more details about
the show than any of the other confirmed Disney+

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:30.860
MCU series.

00:02:30.860 --> 00:02:34.810
The following month Deadline reported Falcon
and Winter Soldier would be six episodes long

00:02:34.810 --> 00:02:39.290
and that director Kari Skogland, known for
her work on The Handmaid's Tale, NOS4A2, and

00:02:39.290 --> 00:02:42.580
The Walking Dead among others, had been recruited
to direct the entire show.

00:02:42.740 --> 00:02:46.740
At the Jus In Bello comic book convention
in Italy, Stan hinted the series would give

00:02:46.750 --> 00:02:51.200
Bucky the chance, quote, "to go out there
and have an identity outside of the circumstances

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:51.980
that we've met him through."

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:55.820
Along with naming Skogland as director, Deadline
released other details.

00:02:55.830 --> 00:02:59.890
The site reported Emily Van Camp, who played
Sharon Carter in Captain America: The Winter

00:02:59.890 --> 00:03:04.290
Soldier and Civil War, is in talks to appear
in the series, as well as Daniel Bruhl who

00:03:04.290 --> 00:03:06.090
played Civil War's villain Zemo.

00:03:06.090 --> 00:03:10.740
According to Deadline, the series is scheduled
to be released on Disney+ in August 2020.

00:03:11.860 --> 00:03:16.700
A little over two weeks before the April 2019
release of Avengers: Endgame, Variety reported

00:03:16.700 --> 00:03:20.180
a Hawkeye series starring Jeremy Renner was
in the works for Disney+.

00:03:20.490 --> 00:03:24.200
Few details have been released about the Hawkeye
series, but The Hollywood Reporter says the

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:27.820
show will follow Clint Barton as he passes
the torch to archer hero.

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:31.950
The upcoming series will revolve around Barton
training the younger Kate Bishop to take over

00:03:31.950 --> 00:03:33.150
the mantle of Hawkeye.

00:03:33.150 --> 00:03:37.920
In the comics, Bishop initially takes the
name after Barton dies in the 2004 event Avengers

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:38.500
Disassembled.

00:03:38.680 --> 00:03:42.980
Once Barton returns to the land of the living,
as most people who die in Marvel Comics eventually

00:03:42.980 --> 00:03:44.959
do, both heroes keep the Hawkeye name.

00:03:44.959 --> 00:03:48.490
This has all been covered extensively in the
comics, but as of now, there's no word on

00:03:48.490 --> 00:03:52.840
how Kate Bishop enters Clint Barton's life,
or who will be playing her in the series.

00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:58.760
In mid-April 2019, a rumor circulated that
Marvel was developing a Hulk/She-Hulk series

00:03:58.760 --> 00:04:01.980
with Mark Ruffalo reprising his role as Bruce
Banner/The Hulk.

00:04:02.180 --> 00:04:04.420
"I put the brains and the brawn together.

00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:06.180
And now look at me.

00:04:07.220 --> 00:04:08.200
Best of both worlds."

00:04:09.240 --> 00:04:12.820
According to the story, She-Hulk would ultimately
be the focus of the series.

00:04:12.820 --> 00:04:15.740
In the comics, She-Hulk is Bruce Banner's
cousin Jennifer Walters.

00:04:15.880 --> 00:04:19.040
Banner inadvertently creates She-Hulk after
his cousin is shot.

00:04:19.040 --> 00:04:22.790
With no other viable donors available, he's
forced to perform a blood transfusion and

00:04:22.790 --> 00:04:24.980
give his own Hulk-infected blood to his cousin.

00:04:25.120 --> 00:04:28.680
Since the initial rumor broke, not many details
have surfaced about the series.

00:04:28.820 --> 00:04:33.160
However, since the release of Avengers: Endgame,
we now know the Hulk, whose right arm is rendered

00:04:33.160 --> 00:04:37.050
permanently damaged after using the Infinity
Stones, probably won't be doing a lot more

00:04:37.050 --> 00:04:38.050
superhero stuff.

00:04:38.050 --> 00:04:41.850
So, if the rumors about the series are true,
it could be that Hulk will find himself much

00:04:41.850 --> 00:04:46.120
in the same position as Hawkeye in his series,
teaching a new hero to fill his shoes.

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:52.120
In February 2019, while promoting Captain
Marvel, Marvel Studios chief Kevin Feige told

00:04:52.130 --> 00:04:57.540
Collider the upcoming Disney+ MCU series would
be important to the, quote, "entire post-Endgame

00:04:57.540 --> 00:04:58.040
MCU."

00:04:58.180 --> 00:05:02.040
Feige also said the series were all conceived
together, and that they would be intertwined

00:05:02.040 --> 00:05:04.380
with each other, as well as the studio's movies.

00:05:04.500 --> 00:05:08.320
Now that Avengers: Endgame has been released,
along with Spider-Man: Far from Home's final

00:05:08.320 --> 00:05:11.760
trailer, we know some of the things that are
different in the MCU since Endgame.

00:05:12.140 --> 00:05:13.520
"This is Mr. Beck."

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:16.240
"We could use someone like you on my world."

00:05:16.240 --> 00:05:16.740
"Your world?"

00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:18.760
"Beck is from Earth, just not ours."

00:05:19.190 --> 00:05:23.140
In particular, we now know that the Earth
of the MCU is connected to a vast multiverse

00:05:23.150 --> 00:05:27.180
of alternate timelines, which are now apparently
much more connected than they used to be ever

00:05:27.180 --> 00:05:28.480
since Thanos' big snap.

00:05:28.760 --> 00:05:31.780
Parallel worlds bring up potentially limitless
possibilities.

00:05:31.920 --> 00:05:35.610
It's probably why a once-dead Loki will be
able to lead his own series, and it could

00:05:35.610 --> 00:05:39.680
also be why the supposedly dead Vision and
the freshly revived Scarlet Witch will be

00:05:39.680 --> 00:05:41.520
back together again in WandaVision.

